1
00:05:53,684 --> 00:05:59,684
In a world on the brink of war. You either march
to one tune or dance to another.

2
00:11:47,368 --> 00:11:53,368
Swing Kids is a music, drama film directed by Thomas Carter.

3
00:17:41,052 --> 00:17:47,052
The story of a close-knit group of young kids in Nazi Germany
who listen to banned swing music from the US.

4
00:23:34,736 --> 00:23:40,736
Soon dancing and fun leads to more difficult choices as the
Nazis begin tightening the grip on Germany.

5
00:29:28,421 --> 00:29:34,421
Each member of the group is forced to face some tough
choices about right, wrong, and survival.

6
00:35:22,105 --> 00:35:28,105
Peter Müller, played by Robert Sean Leonard.

7
00:41:15,789 --> 00:41:21,789
Thomas Berger, played by Christian Bale.

8
00:47:09,473 --> 00:47:15,473
Arvid, played by Frank Whaley.

9
00:53:03,157 --> 00:53:09,157
Frau Müller, played by Barbara Hershey.

10
00:58:56,842 --> 00:59:02,842
Evey, played by Tushka Bergen.

11
01:04:50,526 --> 01:04:56,526
Willi Müller, played by David Tom.

12
01:10:44,210 --> 01:10:50,210
Swing Kids is a 1993 American historical drama film directed by Thomas Carter in his feature film debut, and
starring Robert Sean Leonard, Christian Bale, Frank Whaley, Barbara Hershey and Kenneth Branagh.

13
01:16:37,894 --> 01:16:43,894
The title refers to a youth subculture in Nazi Germany, in which teenagers embraced
American and British swing music in defiance of the Nazi regime.

14
01:22:31,578 --> 01:22:37,578
The film follows two high school students in their attempt to be swing kids by night and
Hitler Youth by day, a decision that acutely impacts their friends and families.

15
01:28:25,263 --> 01:28:31,263
The film was released by Buena Vista Pictures on March 5, 1993.

16
01:34:18,947 --> 01:34:24,947
It received mixed reviews from critics.

17
01:40:12,631 --> 01:40:18,631
The film explores themes of suicide, world war ii,
antisemitism, anti-nazi resistance, swing dancing.

18
01:46:06,315 --> 01:46:12,315
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
